{
  "$description": "F30 Highlights: the shared offsets fixtures (SPEC F30). The backend's block plain text, and the web's and mobile's selection → { blockId, startOffset, endOffset, text } mapping must all agree with this file; each side has a test that reads it. Generated by the backend builder; edit by hand only together with the backend test.",
  "rules": [
    "Offsets are UTF-16 code units (JavaScript and Dart String.length / index) in the block's plain text; startOffset inclusive, endOffset exclusive.",
    "A block's plain text: its inline nodes in order; text, term and mention nodes give their `text` (a mention gives its \"@username\" text), a hardBreak gives \"\\n\". Marks (bold, italic, code, link, highlight, strike) add nothing.",
    "A list (bulletList, orderedList): its items' texts joined by one \"\\n\". Each item is its own unit: a highlight stays inside one item.",
    "Callout title, quote cite, the summary label and list bullets or numbers are not part of the plain text and never part of a highlight.",
    "Highlightable blocks: paragraph, heading, bulletList and orderedList items, quote, callout, summary. Never: code, codeTabs, table, steps, image, divider, embed.",
    "Isolate and embedding characters a renderer inserts (U+2066–U+2069, U+202A–U+202E) never count. The server strips them from stored content, so the plain text never holds them.",
    "A selection is clipped to the first block (list: the first item) it touches. If that block can't be highlighted, there is no toolbar.",
    "Whitespace at both ends is trimmed (the characters in `whitespace`). What is left must be 3–1,000 code units; else no Highlight button (too_short) or the too_long error.",
    "Never normalize text (no NFC, no Arabic normalization, no trimming inside): `text` is exactly plainText.slice(startOffset, endOffset)."
  ],
  "whitespace": "U+0009–U+000D, U+0020, U+0085, U+00A0, U+1680, U+2000–U+200A, U+2028, U+2029, U+202F, U+205F, U+3000",
  "positions": "A selection end is { block, item?, inline, offset }: `item` = the list item index (lists only), `inline` = the index of the inline node in the block's content (or the item), `offset` = UTF-16 offset in that node's text (a hardBreak: 0 before, 1 after). The end of node i is the same point as the start of node i + 1. { block, part, offset } is a point outside the plain text: part \"title\" (callout title), \"cite\" (quote cite), \"code\" / \"cell\" / \"step\" (inside a block that can't be highlighted; the exact point doesn't matter). `anchor` is where the selection began, `focus` where it ended (focus before anchor = a backwards selection).",
